    {
      "game": "Donut County",
      "game_image": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/products/10103/450x258/donut-county-pc-mac-game-steam-cover.jpg?v=1794402000",
      "game_url": "https://www.instant-gaming.com/en/10103-buy-donut-county-pc-mac-game-steam/",
      "user": "SambaL",
      "avatar": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/avatars/27742514-1746025891.jpg",
      "sentiment": "dislike",
      "content": "I didn't like it all that much. It has a pleasant esthetic going for it with a bit of humor, but that's about it. It's way too 'cosy' of a game for me with there being very little challenge to the gameplay. Plus it's quite short. \n\n\n\nBut apparently a lot of people seem to like it so for the little money it costs it might be worth a try for you."
    },
    {
      "game": "Call of Duty: Modern Warfare 4",
      "game_image": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/products/23337/450x258/call-of-duty-modern-warfare-4-switch-2-nintendo-eshop-cover.jpg?v=1794402000",
      "game_url": "https://www.instant-gaming.com/en/23337-buy-call-of-duty-modern-warfare-4-switch-2-nintendo-eshop/",
      "user": "gamer-9aa6f1d",
      "avatar": "https://gaming-cdn.com/themes/igv2/images/avatar2.svg",
      "sentiment": "like",
      "content": "For casual campaign mode in handheld mode it's fun. Multiplayer only in 1080p and aiming by joy-con mouse mode its also fun. 4k its not for this hardware though. General experience is good. Nice variety to switch platform."
    },
    {
      "game": "The Blood of Dawnwalker",
      "game_image": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/products/15628/450x258/the-blood-of-dawnwalker-pc-steam-cover.jpg?v=1794402000",
      "game_url": "https://www.instant-gaming.com/en/15628-buy-the-blood-of-dawnwalker-pc-steam/",
      "user": "summ0n3r",
      "avatar": "https://gaming-cdn.com/themes/igv2/images/avatar2.svg",
      "sentiment": "like",
      "content": "Taking into account all the good things and bad things, I still enjoyed the game very much and would recommend it.\n\n\n\nIt is difficult not to compare this game to its obvious inspiration, The Witcher, and quite frankly it does not live up to it, which is fine considering the difference between two studios that created the games.\n\n\n\nThe game starts extremely good and interesting but then it comes to a bit of a repetitive chore that progresses the story bit by bit. This improves significantly towards the end which gives out an impression that the team had a good idea but did not really know how to execute it and make the game consistently interesting. Side quests are a very obvious example as they are really not on the level I expected.\n\n\n\nI do expect to come back to this game once again in the future once the development team has finished ironing out the wrinkles, and hopefully does some improvements with the content."
    }
